WEBVTT

00:01.560 --> 00:05.190
Only the undead can see this lantern's light.

00:05.190 --> 00:08.650
And in the eyes of those who have lost
 their reason through neglect,

00:08.650 --> 00:10.800
it outshines all else.

00:12.610 --> 00:15.910
I chose a deserted area 
to minimize the risk,

00:16.700 --> 00:19.870
but it appears we unintentionally 
hit the nail on the head.

00:21.030 --> 00:23.680
Oh, the trail keeps going this way.

00:28.440 --> 00:30.480
With necromancy,

00:31.500 --> 00:34.950
no parting lasts forever.

00:39.200 --> 00:40.640
What have you done?

00:41.770 --> 00:43.680
What have you done?!

00:44.350 --> 00:47.140
This will suffice for him,

00:47.140 --> 00:52.990
but as for you, woman, despite my efforts,
 I couldn't learn a thing about you.

00:52.990 --> 00:56.960
I'll avail myself of a bargaining chip now.

01:03.750 --> 01:04.790
Johan!

01:06.400 --> 01:10.090
Do as I say, and you'll see him again soon.

01:10.560 --> 01:12.940
Now, follow me.

03:20.870 --> 03:25.430
Um... Performing her autopsy 
must be hard for you.

03:25.960 --> 03:27.190
Why don't I take over?

03:28.130 --> 03:29.650
There's no need.

03:30.280 --> 03:32.830
I'm perfectly fine.

03:32.830 --> 03:34.850
Is that so?

03:40.340 --> 03:43.180
How hideous.

03:44.280 --> 03:51.640
Mireille, I shall bring you back
 with flawless beauty.

03:56.790 --> 04:01.630
Beauty and Death: 
Final Act

04:13.860 --> 04:16.380
<i>Despite how she treated Johan,</i>

04:16.380 --> 04:20.070
<i>she must've really cared about him.</i>

04:50.480 --> 04:52.340
Ah, excuse me.

04:52.890 --> 04:55.770
This occasionally happens 
when I disengage Manual.

04:56.630 --> 05:00.750
The undead person's mind
 fails to return, I mean.

05:02.160 --> 05:03.570
Have a seat.

05:07.630 --> 05:11.620
We saw plenty of other 
servants on the way here.

05:11.990 --> 05:14.580
Don't tell me they're <i>all</i> undead?

05:14.870 --> 05:16.540
Indeed they are.

05:19.620 --> 05:21.210
This isn't a one-man crime.

05:21.210 --> 05:23.480
You must have accomplices.

05:23.480 --> 05:28.430
Even I know that resurrecting the 
undead takes a ton of magical energy.

05:28.640 --> 05:32.930
There's no way you could have 
brought back this many on your own.

05:32.930 --> 05:35.320
It is possible, even without help.

05:35.320 --> 05:36.270
What?

05:36.270 --> 05:41.890
Raising complete people and keeping them
 that way with regular maintenance

05:41.890 --> 05:45.990
is what consumes vast amounts of power.

05:47.200 --> 05:53.320
Sloppy work, as seen in the undead in 
that ruin, doesn't take all that much power.

05:53.790 --> 05:55.870
He neglected their maintenance, too.

06:00.930 --> 06:05.170
And while these girls seem 
decent at first glance,

06:05.870 --> 06:08.220
I'm sure they're barely there inside.

06:09.890 --> 06:15.300
Unscrupulous necromancers often do 
the bare minimum for functionality.

06:15.860 --> 06:19.190
They don't bother restoring 
most of the organs or senses.

06:19.720 --> 06:22.150
It takes hardly any magic.

06:23.060 --> 06:24.860
Well spotted.

06:25.750 --> 06:27.490
You know your necromancy.

06:27.760 --> 06:32.450
The question is whether they're strays.

06:34.240 --> 06:38.370
Of course, they're probably 
all strays on Semi-auto.

06:44.270 --> 06:45.550
I'm shocked.

06:46.170 --> 06:48.860
Even you must know how 
sinful creating strays is,

06:48.860 --> 06:54.680
and how heavy a price the 
dead pay for resurrection.

06:55.170 --> 06:56.520
Naturally.

06:57.000 --> 06:58.480
What price?

07:00.690 --> 07:06.460
Normally, after death, the soul 
begins preparing for reincarnation.

07:09.330 --> 07:14.070
Souls flow into the spiral 
of death and rebirth,

07:14.070 --> 07:17.120
and after a long time, 
they achieve resurrection.

07:17.800 --> 07:24.160
But necromancy drags them 
back out of that current.

07:26.580 --> 07:29.010
Magical resurrection doesn't last forever.

07:31.070 --> 07:35.440
When the spell eventually fails 
and they die a second time,

07:35.440 --> 07:37.810
they cannot return to the cycle.

07:39.330 --> 07:43.630
There is no way to rejoin 
the stream after leaving it.

07:44.930 --> 07:50.060
Wandering souls go somewhere that 
has no up or down. No left or right.

07:50.060 --> 07:54.780
No motion or pain. 
No light or sound or heat.

07:55.470 --> 07:57.830
Their minds simply exist.

07:58.360 --> 08:01.120
And nothing changes for eternity.

08:02.450 --> 08:04.450
That hell is called...

08:05.830 --> 08:06.960
the Void.

08:08.180 --> 08:13.220
So all undead go there? 
They all fall into the Void?

08:13.220 --> 08:14.960
Sooner or later.

08:24.390 --> 08:28.000
To accept death and await reincarnation,

08:28.000 --> 08:33.560
or to regain a temporary life in exchange 
for a fate crueler than death?

08:34.170 --> 08:39.870
You deprived them of the right 
to make that crucial decision.

08:40.990 --> 08:43.760
Let the undead worry about that.

08:43.760 --> 08:46.750
It doesn't affect necromancers.

08:47.640 --> 08:49.130
You piece of shit!

08:49.130 --> 08:53.900
What the hell did you do this for?!
 What could justify your atrocities?!

08:54.360 --> 08:56.160
My goal?

08:57.070 --> 08:58.720
Let me think...

08:59.260 --> 09:01.060
Put simply,

09:01.060 --> 09:02.340
it's you.

09:02.850 --> 09:05.540
I want your beauty.

09:06.750 --> 09:13.150
You see, I lost someone I loved, 
just like both of you did.

09:16.350 --> 09:17.820
What beauty.

09:18.310 --> 09:24.310
She was a beautiful young 
woman with fiery red hair.

09:25.770 --> 09:30.000
Fortunately, I had my necromancy.

09:30.270 --> 09:34.300
Reuniting with her should 
have been a simple matter.

09:34.520 --> 09:40.940
But unfortunately, the manner of her 
death burned away most of her skin.

09:41.600 --> 09:45.040
I can produce any number 
of hideous creatures.

09:45.040 --> 09:48.310
Beauty, however, is challenging to recreate.

09:48.820 --> 09:54.740
Still, I need only gather those 
who still have what she lost.

09:55.000 --> 09:58.950
I can supplement any 
remaining deficiencies myself.

10:01.040 --> 10:03.870
Beautiful things appeal to me.

10:03.870 --> 10:10.170
I might as well give her the loveliest 
possible body when I resurrect her.

10:10.870 --> 10:15.560
I practiced on those corpses you 
saw to improve my technique.

10:15.560 --> 10:18.300
Sometimes more successfully than others.

10:19.210 --> 10:20.780
That's it?

10:21.690 --> 10:24.010
That's your only reason?

10:24.650 --> 10:28.520
Everyone values things differently.

10:28.850 --> 10:30.430
What do you think?

10:30.430 --> 10:36.030
All the undead and taxidermy specimens 
in this room represent my successes.

10:36.760 --> 10:39.740
I think they came out well. And yet...

10:40.050 --> 10:43.020
They pale beside your beauty.

10:43.960 --> 10:49.670
I do hope you'll let me 
use your body as a base.

10:55.530 --> 10:56.920
How dull.

10:58.180 --> 11:00.630
That's really your only reason?

11:00.990 --> 11:05.480
I played along because 
I expected there to be more to it.

11:05.480 --> 11:06.890
Ms. Kristoffel...

11:06.890 --> 11:08.880
Such composure.

11:08.880 --> 11:13.450
I see. Given your knowledge of resurrection,

11:13.450 --> 11:17.020
you must be a necromancer, too.

11:17.750 --> 11:24.780
I wondered why the undead I'd abandoned 
underground ran off all of a sudden.

11:24.780 --> 11:28.500
I suppose that was your doing.

11:28.800 --> 11:33.910
But even if you are a necromancer, 
what can you do in this situation?

11:33.910 --> 11:37.340
You abide by the rules, don't you?

11:39.530 --> 11:42.230
As long as rules bind you,

11:42.230 --> 11:44.440
you cannot oppose me.

11:45.510 --> 11:48.770
Please don't try to be clever.

11:58.100 --> 11:59.360
Sorry...

12:00.530 --> 12:03.160
but I'm not <i>just</i> a necromancer.

12:04.570 --> 12:05.990
Your eyes!

12:06.480 --> 12:08.030
Those runes!

12:14.830 --> 12:17.000
No... It can't be...

12:22.160 --> 12:23.120
A witch!

12:26.530 --> 12:28.720
I wasted my tears.

12:34.480 --> 12:35.680
Impossible!

12:35.680 --> 12:40.230
How could I have unwittingly 
invited a witch here?

12:40.230 --> 12:42.870
<i>A witch? No way.</i>

12:43.450 --> 12:46.780
<i>But come to think of it, it makes sense.</i>

12:47.420 --> 12:54.350
<i>Since I first set eyes on her, her beauty 
has seemed chilling, almost otherworldly.</i>

12:54.830 --> 12:58.670
So I take it we're going 
to do this the hard way?

12:59.000 --> 13:00.250
Of course.

13:00.250 --> 13:03.470
Wait. You seem to have forgotten something.

13:03.790 --> 13:07.510
Why do you think I took a hostage?

13:09.280 --> 13:13.440
You can't resurrect someone 
without a part of their corpse.

13:13.440 --> 13:18.520
If I have my undead reduce him 
to ash, you'll never see him a—

13:18.520 --> 13:20.070
Suit yourself.

13:21.390 --> 13:23.620
He won't make a good hostage.

13:24.130 --> 13:25.450
And regardless,

13:25.770 --> 13:30.410
I won't stop until I've dealt with you.

13:31.840 --> 13:33.840
I see.

13:33.840 --> 13:38.080
Then it seems I must resort to force.

13:43.460 --> 13:46.740
"Prepare for the worst," and all that.

13:47.700 --> 13:51.270
Thank goodness I made combat models.

13:52.340 --> 13:54.140
Combat models?

13:54.500 --> 13:56.600
Don't you ever stop?

13:56.990 --> 14:02.070
I don't know how much you tinkered 
with them, but they're merely strays.

14:02.800 --> 14:05.500
You can bind them with Semi-auto,

14:05.500 --> 14:11.280
but they remain mindless automatons, 
barely aware of themselves.

14:11.690 --> 14:13.740
You can't beat me with those.

14:14.880 --> 14:16.250
You're bluffing.

14:17.030 --> 14:22.020
Few people wish to become undead 
knowing they'll fall into the Void.

14:22.880 --> 14:29.510
Even fewer would put themselves 
in a necromancer's service or control.

14:29.510 --> 14:32.970
But even knowing everything,

14:33.400 --> 14:36.680
some still offer themselves
 to necromancers.

14:37.950 --> 14:39.940
With the utmost respect, I call them...

14:43.610 --> 14:45.390
Death Knights.

14:50.190 --> 14:54.780
None of you lay a hand 
on that bearded man.

14:55.750 --> 14:57.660
As for everyone else, well...

14:58.280 --> 15:00.370
Do as you please.

15:15.060 --> 15:15.850
Stop!

15:16.770 --> 15:17.850
Don't fight!

15:18.070 --> 15:20.270
P-Please stop!

15:34.090 --> 15:35.160
Sorry.

15:35.690 --> 15:41.620
As long as the spell lasts, killing the 
body is the only way to stop them.

15:44.760 --> 15:48.460
I'll see to it that the 
necromancer gets his just deserts.

15:56.590 --> 15:58.380
What a miscalculation!

15:58.380 --> 16:00.950
Why a witch, of all people?

16:00.950 --> 16:02.890
Damn, damn, damn, damn!

16:03.280 --> 16:06.170
How dare she ruin my plans?!

16:07.810 --> 16:09.190
But I'm not finished.

16:09.650 --> 16:14.860
I'll remodel your body into 
the ultimate warrior right now.

16:16.800 --> 16:18.640
Man, seriously?

16:18.640 --> 16:20.580
What a scumbag.

16:23.730 --> 16:29.170
What happened to all that talk about beauty?

16:29.170 --> 16:32.260
Impossible! How are you alive?

16:32.620 --> 16:36.720
Oh, no. I'm good and dead.

16:36.940 --> 16:39.080
When did the witch resurrect you?

16:39.080 --> 16:41.850
She was with me until just a moment ago!

16:41.850 --> 16:43.420
She had no time to—

16:43.420 --> 16:47.940
Oh, come on. What's so weird about it?

16:48.750 --> 16:53.570
I've been undead this whole time.

16:55.250 --> 17:00.620
But undead can't get over physical death
 without necromantic maintenance.

17:01.270 --> 17:05.870
So how am I standing here
 good as new, you ask?

17:06.890 --> 17:09.340
The answer to that should be obvious.

17:09.600 --> 17:13.670
I'm not just any undead.

17:16.000 --> 17:19.000
I'm a <i>witch's</i> undead.

17:20.720 --> 17:22.470
S-Stay back!

17:22.470 --> 17:23.480
Stop!

17:29.800 --> 17:31.150
Basically...

17:33.640 --> 17:35.640
I'm built different.

17:36.470 --> 17:37.650
Wait!

17:37.650 --> 17:40.160
Calm down, now. Don't kill me.

17:40.160 --> 17:42.080
Don't kill me!

17:42.080 --> 17:44.830
If you kill me, all of those undead will...

17:45.250 --> 17:46.460
Kill you?

17:47.050 --> 17:50.040
Nah, I'm not gonna kill you.

17:50.330 --> 17:53.760
See, you crossed a line.

17:54.440 --> 17:57.270
You broke every taboo in the book.

17:57.270 --> 17:59.300
I... I know.

17:59.620 --> 18:03.350
I'll take responsibility for those undead.

18:03.350 --> 18:06.380
You pissed off Phanora.

18:06.810 --> 18:09.980
Death's way too good for you.

18:10.320 --> 18:11.910
S-Stop...

18:13.090 --> 18:15.570
I'll start with your fingers.

18:15.860 --> 18:17.280
Please stop!

18:17.810 --> 18:19.530
I-I beg—

18:33.070 --> 18:35.920
Johan, you...

18:37.390 --> 18:39.300
I haven't killed him yet.

18:44.360 --> 18:45.280
Listen.

18:45.280 --> 18:46.390
Y-Yes?

18:46.390 --> 18:52.440
I'm about to break the law, so could you
 keep this whole incident to yourself?

18:52.440 --> 18:53.270
What?

18:53.580 --> 18:55.290
A promise won't do.

18:55.800 --> 18:58.240
You'll need to consent to a contract spell.

18:58.520 --> 19:00.140
I don't know...

19:00.140 --> 19:05.500
The Order of Magical Resonance remains 
shrouded in mystery despite its fame

19:05.500 --> 19:08.490
because we require our clients 
to watch their words.

19:08.490 --> 19:11.580
You want me to turn a blind eye
 to a crime? I could never—

19:11.580 --> 19:14.750
Don't you want to save her?

19:15.870 --> 19:18.300
If you want to save all the victims,

19:19.510 --> 19:22.010
shut up and do as I say.

19:35.700 --> 19:42.030
I'll have you maintain all the undead 
you resurrected as complete human beings.

19:44.140 --> 19:48.520
I'll provide the magical power,
 so don't slack off.

19:49.270 --> 19:51.870
What have you done?

19:52.160 --> 19:54.830
What have you done?!

19:54.830 --> 19:56.840
Me, undead?

19:56.840 --> 19:59.960
How dare you?! How <i>dare</i> you?!

19:59.960 --> 20:03.840
This means I'll... I'll fall into the Void, and—

20:05.480 --> 20:07.500
Worrying about the afterlife already?

20:08.250 --> 20:11.460
I hate to break it to you,

20:11.460 --> 20:16.230
but I won't give you a moment's peace 
while you're in <i>this</i> world, either.

20:19.260 --> 20:24.490
Ms. Kristoffel, does this mean
 I can see her again?

20:26.510 --> 20:28.920
The way she used to be?

20:30.710 --> 20:31.960
Well, yes.

20:32.240 --> 20:36.030
Her illegal resurrection means she'll 
have to keep a low profile for now,

20:36.630 --> 20:40.170
but I know ways to legitimize her.

20:41.620 --> 20:43.180
Is that so?

20:44.080 --> 20:45.290
Feeling conflicted?

20:46.440 --> 20:47.640
I guess so.

20:48.380 --> 20:49.930
I feel torn,

20:50.620 --> 20:53.880
but thoughtless as it is, 
I can't help being happy.

21:00.170 --> 21:01.030
Hey.

21:01.490 --> 21:02.190
What?

21:02.440 --> 21:04.510
You're done now, right, Phanora?

21:04.510 --> 21:05.780
Get away from him.

21:06.000 --> 21:07.140
You're too close.

21:09.380 --> 21:10.240
Johan.

21:10.490 --> 21:11.450
Yeah?

21:11.790 --> 21:15.160
What did you do with my luggage?

21:15.160 --> 21:15.920
Huh?

21:16.770 --> 21:17.630
Uh, wait.

21:18.180 --> 21:19.950
Where'd I put it?

21:19.950 --> 21:21.410
Are you saying you lost it?

21:21.410 --> 21:23.110
I mean, I had more important things—

21:23.110 --> 21:24.610
Find it.

21:25.300 --> 21:26.470
Fine.

21:27.580 --> 21:29.030
Not even a thank you.

21:29.910 --> 21:31.070
Johan.

21:31.070 --> 21:32.780
Yeah? What do you want?

21:34.560 --> 21:35.980
I'm sorry.

21:37.060 --> 21:42.230
I spoke thoughtlessly without 
realizing you were undead.

21:42.230 --> 21:45.900
And I warned you to 
"watch out for beautiful women,"

21:46.520 --> 21:50.120
but you never had a choice, did you?

21:51.400 --> 21:54.230
Do I look that unfortunate to you?

21:54.230 --> 21:56.180
You don't seem well-treated.

21:58.030 --> 22:00.130
That figures.

22:00.760 --> 22:01.880
But whatever.

22:02.660 --> 22:03.850
Don't worry.

22:04.770 --> 22:06.670
This is fine by me.

22:17.920 --> 22:19.500
Wh-What are you doing?!

22:19.990 --> 22:21.610
What do you mean?

22:25.150 --> 22:27.540
That was for hurting Johan.

24:01.360 --> 24:03.960
I haven't even had a boyfriend yet!

24:04.910 --> 24:09.960
Next time: "The Witch and 
the Demon Sword: Opening Act."

24:06.000 --> 24:09.960
The Witch and the Demon Sword

24:06.000 --> 24:09.960
Opening Act
